# Feature parity contract (do not break)

Train/serve skew is the top failure mode this design avoids. Enforce it:

- Every feature lives ONLY in `rba-features` as a pure function of
  `(event, profile_state)` — never read global/current-time state, never re-implement
  a feature in another repo/language.
- `compute_features(event, profile)` reads only its two args. `update_profile(...)` is
  called AFTER compute, so the current event never leaks into its own vector.
- Offline (replay) and online (materialised profile) paths MUST produce identical
  vectors. Any change to features/profile requires updating `tests/test_parity.py`
  and keeping it green.
- Missing values (`"-"`, NaN, empty) must NEVER count as "seen before" and must not be
  added to a profile's seen-set.

## Excluded on purpose (EDA-justified — don't silently re-add)

- `rtt_deviation` — RTT is ~94% missing.
- absolute km / city-level geo / GPS as Freeman inputs — geo is synthesised
  and region/city are ~42% missing. Prefer `*_seen_before` signals.

## Allowed as a PDP rule, not a Freeman feature (ADR-0022)

- Country-centroid `impossible_travel` may live in `rba-features` as
  `f(event, profile)` and **escalate** the policy action. Same centroid table
  offline and online; missing country never fires; VPN/hosting ASNs skip
  teleport. Do not implement GPS or city GeoIP as a model input.
